 "note": {
  "status": "draft",
  "text": "Computer maintenance keeps a computer working well and for a long time.\n• Preventive maintenance (before problems): dust the computer and keyboard; keep it cool and ventilated; use a surge protector or stabiliser and a UPS (inverter) against power cuts; update the operating system and antivirus; delete unneeded files; back up data; shut down properly.\n• Corrective maintenance (after a problem): find the cause and repair it — replace a faulty part, reinstall software, remove a virus.\nSafety: switch off and unplug before opening or cleaning; avoid static electricity (touch metal first); never pour liquids near the computer; keep food and drinks away.\nA UPS (uninterruptible power supply) gives a few minutes of power after a cut so you can save your work.",
  "checks": []
 },
 "worked_example": {
  "status": "draft",
  "vars": {},
  "problem": "Why is a UPS useful in places with frequent power cuts?",
  "steps": [
   "A sudden power cut can damage files and parts.",
   "A UPS gives battery power for a few minutes so you can save your work and shut down properly."
  ],
  "answer": "It gives time to save work and shut down safely.",
  "checks": []
 },
